I'm looking into managing cardinality by limiting the number of active series per tenant and considering methods like active series tracking and bloom filters. I want to address both write-time validation and query-time protection through query sharding and setting maximum series. Additionally, I’ll focus on using TSDB blocks for storage. My targets are to ingest 10 million samples per second and handle up to 1 million active series per tenant with a retention period of one year. There are also various failure modes I need to account for, like ingester crashes and object storage outages. I should also include operational notes regarding rollouts and backpressure. Lastly, I’ll remember that YAML front matter needs titles and tags. Let's get to writing!
